Hi,

Yes, the talk you reference is about SELinux -- related to the work on 
finding and evaluating a minimal trusted computing base from the SELinux 
example policy that was discussed on this list a while back.

Since the USENIX conference is in DC, we should probably plan some sort of 
BoF or some other SELinux-related get together.  Do folks have a 
preference?

Regards,
Trent.
